#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# parametric_nd_solve_value

#% text
# `parametric_nd_solve_value(eqs, expr, [t, t0, t1], [p1, ..., pm])` gives `expr` along the numerical solution of `eqs` as a function of the parameters `p1, ..., pm`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is another name of `parametric_n_dsolve_value`; the result `f` is a parametric function, and `f(v1, ..., vm)` the value with the parameters set to the numbers `v1, ..., vm`.

#% item
# `find_root` and `plot` can use `f(a)` of a symbolic parameter: the call waits for a number.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
f = parametric_nd_solve_value([y''(t) + a*y(t) == 0, y(0) == 1, y'(0) == 0], y(10), [t, 0, 10], [a])

#% cell
f(1)
#% output
#= -0.8390715009436508

#% cell
find_root(f(a), [a, 1])
#% output
#= [a -> 1.2090265378821354]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `parametric_nd_solve`, `parametric_n_dsolve_value`, `find_root`
